1170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1136 0 R
/E (  We drew inspiration from arcade dance rhythm games and Whac-A-Mole, both of which rely on quick reaction, timing, and physical interaction. From the dance arcade game, we adopted the idea of following illuminated directions in sync with music. From Whac-A-Mole, we borrowed the concept of reacting instantly to randomly appearing cues. We then translated these large, physical arcade experiences into a compact, sensor-based version using an ESP32. By replacing full-scale floor panels with directional touch inputs and LED indicators, we retained the energy and responsiveness of arcade gameplay while making it minimal, portable, and technically achievable within our project constraints.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
